{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3369","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3369","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3369\",\"parent_revision\":\"068853c80a187998d94a9ada8fe0aa73187a010c\",\"root_revision\":\"5cb6c4b52129a8a54316e48fd746746757f50d11002c6892abb73c893c5eef09\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-01\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPR #3367 typed 42 of `backlog_core/server.py`'s 43 MCP tools with real Pydantic response models. Every tool follows the same return pattern: `SomeResponse.model_validate({...}).model_dump(exclude_none=True)`. This exact two-call chain is copy-pasted verbatim at roughly 40 call sites (89 `model_validate` calls total, 71 followed by the identical `.model_dump(exclude_none=True)`).\\n\\nTwo tools are deliberate exceptions to the pattern: `sync_status`/`sync_now` build their response without `exclude_none=True`, because every field in `SyncState.to_dict()` is unconditionally present and some legitimately carry a `null` value that must stay in the wire payload (see `test_sync_status_returns_all_required_fields`, and the fix in PR #3367 for `backlog_get_soonest_milestone`, which had the same class of bug \u2014 a documented, meaningful `None` silently dropped by blanket `exclude_none=True`). Right now these two exceptions are distinguished from the other ~40 call sites only by a code comment, not by any structural signal.\\n\\nRisk this creates: a future contributor adding tool #44 (or modifying one of the existing 42) copies one of the ~40 standard call sites, and is exactly as likely to accidentally omit `exclude_none=True` where it's needed, or include it where a field's `None` is meaningful data (as already happened once with `backlog_get_soonest_milestone`), since nothing forces the choice to be deliberate.\\n\\nProposed fix: a small helper \u2014 e.g. `def _respond(cls: type[BaseModel], payload: dict[str, object], *, exclude_none: bool = True) -> dict[str, object]: return cls.model_validate(payload).model_dump(exclude_none=exclude_none)` \u2014 used at all ~40 standard call sites, with the two exceptions passing `exclude_none=False` explicitly rather than by omission. This makes \\\"this tool has a load-bearing null\\\" a visible, searchable, one-keyword decision instead of a pattern a future author has to remember to deviate from.\\n\\nNot done in #3367 itself: this is a mechanical but wide-reaching refactor (~40 call sites in an already very large PR); tracked here rather than expanding that PR's scope further.\\n\\nAcceptance criteria:\\n- [ ] A shared `_respond()` (or equivalently named) helper exists in `backlog_core/server.py` (or `tool_responses.py`) wrapping `model_validate(...).model_dump(exclude_none=...)`.\\n- [ ] All ~40 standard call sites use it.\\n- [ ] `sync_status`/`sync_now` (and any other legitimate `exclude_none=False` case) pass that explicitly, not by omission.\\n- [ ] Full `plugins/development-harness` test suite and `tests/test_tool_output_schemas.py` still green; `ruff check`/`ty check` clean.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from PR #3367 (FastMCP typed-output rollout), suggested by /code-review high --fix\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Grooming Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-01T08:47:55.383428Z</sub>\\n\\nTwo corrections to the item's stated rationale, found before implementing:\\n\\n1. The helper's return type must be a `TypeVar` bound to `BaseModel` (`-> M`),\\n   not `-> dict[str, object]` / `-> dict[str, Any]`. Probed all four candidate\\n   signatures against `ty` (this repo's type checker) with a minimal repro: every\\n   tool is annotated `-> SomeResponse` but its body returns a dict today, which\\n   `ty` accepts inline but NOT through a helper annotated to return a dict --\\n   that breaks all ~73 call sites. `-> M` (matching the model class passed in)\\n   keeps `ty` clean and preserves call-site type information; `-> Any` also\\n   passes but throws away that information.\\n\\n2. `sync_status`/`sync_now` are not \\\"exclude_none=True omitted\\\" cases as\\n   described -- they never call `.model_dump()` at all; they return the\\n   `SyncStatusResponse`/`SyncNowResponse` model instance directly\\n   (`server.py:1207`'s comment explains why: FastMCP serializes a returned\\n   model instance identically to a dumped dict at the wire boundary, so no\\n   `exclude_none` question even arises). They are simply out of scope for this\\n   helper, not an `exclude_none=False` call site as the item implies. The real\\n   exclude_none=False-by-necessity population is smaller than described: one\\n   `exclude_defaults=True` site (`backlog_list` count_only, `:1792`) and ~4-5\\n   validate-then-patch-the-dump sites (milestones/soonest-milestone/issues\\n   responses that need the model instance's typed fields AND a mutated dump).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"65202f4bb802de33d5c39b64e5de5327e224c3eb5b539cf4740ffd798364e85f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABR4NNfA\"}"}